2. The raw 132-variable current polynomial of that row reduces, by exact sparse division and original-row replay, through original first rows and **exactly one** original previous `X-1` row, to the scalar `-N13`. Pole original rows are not N13 summands. Quadratic source rows are retained; the linear packer is used only on reduced echelon / affine first-band rows.
